Provenance caveat
-----------------
The design lineage runs through the GitHub repository jday96314/QuantumAI. Every public
note on it says it "states no license", and it returned HTTP 404 on 2026-10-29. Alex
Chilton's notebook says his decoder was rebuilt from that repository's code. SomeJoint
describes its decoder as rebuilt from scratch, starting from Chilton's design, and
licenses its code as Apache-2.0. We could not compare the ported text with jday96314's
code.

Our own files (Apache-2.0)
--------------------------
generate.py, __init__.py, MANIFEST.json, NOTICE, .gitattributes. generate.py
re-implements the upstream build script (pro_q2_897/build_897.py, which we do not run)
with the same register layout and output format, plus a manifest check and a JSON build
record.

kickmix (the circuit builder the code runs on) is Google's, under its own licence; it is
not part of this directory.
